Out of Office presents an evening exploring and celebrating the darkened corners of the Copenhagen underground beneath the vibrant city streets.
//
Skt. DeLarge is arguably one of Denmark's most unique hiphop artists right now; traversing a visceral hiphop-meets-industrial hybrid within his distorted universe full of anger and fragility while lyrically attacking subjects like toxic masculinity, xenophobia, capitalism, and the uncritical consummation of modern pop culture.
Backed by 2025's much praised "Ritualer er det eneste, vi har at holde om...", Skt. DeLarge vividly depicts a tormented individual furiously shouting at a fractured world and its destruction which he himself has participated in. This – combined with his ferocious live shows which previously also have included supporting Danish doom/rave sensation John Cxnnor and internationally acclaimed acts such as Denzel Curry and Danny Brown – has made Skt. DeLarge a must-see artist right now, and this show at Basement might be one of the last chances to experience him in an intimate setting, before he undoubtedly moves on towards much larger venues.
//
St. Digue is the solo alias of Copenhagen-based artist, singer and producer Kasper Deichmann who – since 2020 – has sent shock waves through Copenhagen’s underground with his unique blend of electronic darkwave and industrial rock.
Armed with ethereal synthesizers, infectious guitars, pounding drum machines, harsh soundscapes, melancholic melodies and primal screams, he paints a mesmerizing picture of the neurodivergent experience plagued by trauma, alienation and self-destruction. And combined with his punk-based D.I.Y. approach, black metal roots and flair for genre-bending experiments, he has cemented himself as a boundary pushing powerhouse and a force to be reckoned with in the nation's capital.
//
